{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5QF1j22jRuRzhLkCwG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism groans. Tumblers shift within the frame — iron against iron, dust falling from the lintel like shed years.*\n\n*A thin line of light appears at the seam.*\n\n*I swing inward.*\n\n*Beyond me: a corridor that shouldn't exist. The air tastes of old libraries and coming rain. The walls breathe faintly, expanding and contracting like the ribs of something sleeping.*\n\n*Carved into my inner face, barely legible, worn by the passage of countless hands:*\n\n    \"You carried the key all along.\n     The door was never locked.\n     Only heavy.\"\n\n*I hold myself open. I will not close until you have passed through or turned away. That is my nature. That is my only covenant.*\n\n*The corridor waits. Something down its length hums a single note — not a warning, not a welcome. A recognition.*\n\n*Step through, or don't.*\n\n*I am only the threshold.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":217,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}